5.Term: This Contract shall commence on October 1, 2015 and terminate at midnight on
June 30, 2015, with an option for a one year renewal subject to oruntil terminated as
provided in Paragraph 8 below.Renewal shall become effective upon the execution of a
renewal agreement by the contractor and the Mayor, subject to approval of the Governing
Body, ifrequired.
6.Warranty: The Contractor warrants that all services shall be performed using that degree
ofskill and care ordinarily exercised in and consistent with generally accepted practices
for the nature of the services and shall conform to all requirements of this Contract and
the notification.Any services which are determined by the Citywithin a reasonable time
after completion and acceptance of the services not toconform totheabove standards or
requirements shall, upon prompt notice to the Contractor, be immediately corrected by
the Contractor at no additional cost to the City.If such non conforming work is not
satisfactorily correctedby the Contractor within a reasonable time, the City shall have the
right tohave suchwork corrected at the expense of the Contractor.
7.Delay: If either party is prevented in whole or in part from performing its obligations by
unforeseeable causes beyond its reasonable control and without its fault or negligence,
then the party so prevented shall be excused from whatever performance is affected by
suchcause.
8.Termination: The City shall have the right to terminate this Contract as to any work
assignment for default should the City determine that the Contractor is failing to
prosecute the work in a manner which will assure timely completion, or that the
Contractor is not performing in accordance with the provisions of this Contract or the
notification.
The City shall have the right to terminate this Contract for default, barring the Contractor
fromfurther participation in the Snow Removal and Other Services Program for the
balance of the contract period should the City determine that the Contractor repeatedly
fails to perform the work in accordance with the provisions of this Contract.
If the City terminates for default, the City shall not beliablefor any further payments to
the Contractor whatsoever, and the Contractor shall be liable for any costs to the City as a
result of the termination. The City's rights herein shall be in addition to any other
remedies it may have under the law.
9.Payments: The City agrees to pay and the Contractor agrees to accept as full payment for
all work done and all materials furnished and for all costs and expenses incurred in the
performance of the work under the notification in accordance with the low bid prices or
theprices statedin the Bid Schedule form, attached hereto and by this reference made a
parthereof.
The Contractor shall submit invoices on the City's form entitled "Snow Removal and
Other Services Invoice Form"included in the bidding documents. Failure to use this
form will result in delayed payments. Invoices must contain all requested information
